+# Storage policy: tracer-evaldb 0.0.1
+
+## 1. What this document is
+
+See `packages/evaldb/README.md`, `packages/evaldb/CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/concepts/storage.md`.
+
+The package stores the entities of `tracer-evalschema` 0.0.1 in SQLite or Postgres through the repository functions of `tracer_evaldb` (`test_invalid_run_bundle_never_stored`).
+
+The version is unreleased and nothing is published (unverified).
+
+## 2. The parity table
+
+Both backends store the same value the same way, and the table below is the parity table that `test_storage_policy_parity_table_matches_column_types` compares with the real column types.
+
+| Logical type | Postgres | SQLite (STRICT) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `UuidCol` | `uuid` | `BLOB` |
+| `InstantCol` | `timestamptz` | `TEXT` |
+| `DecimalCol` | `numeric` | `TEXT` |
+| `DocCol` | `text` | `TEXT` |
+| `Sha256Col` | `bytea` | `BLOB` |
+| `KeyCol` | `varchar COLLATE "C"` | `TEXT COLLATE "BINARY"` |
+| `BigIntCol` | `bigint` | `INTEGER` |
+| `BoolCol` | `boolean` | `INTEGER` |
+
+SQLite tables are STRICT and WITHOUT ROWID (`test_sqlite_tables_are_strict_without_rowid`).
+
+## 3. The database is not a validation boundary
+
+The DB is not a validation boundary, the repository is (`test_the_database_accepts_what_the_models_reject_and_verify_database_finds_it`).
+
+- A raw INSERT with a document the models reject is accepted by the database, and the repository refuses to load it (`test_the_database_accepts_what_the_models_reject_and_verify_database_finds_it`).
+- The update triggers refuse every UPDATE of a stored row, and nothing else (`test_update_rejected_on_every_table`).
+- `verify_database` is the admin check that finds such rows and reports kind and ID only (`test_verify_database_finds_tampered_doc`).
+
+## 4. Limits
+
+- Integers are stored in the range plus or minus 2**53 - 1, and a larger value is refused before any write (`test_store_run_bundle_refuses_an_integer_it_cannot_store_before_any_write`).
+- SQLite needs library version 3.37 (`test_sqlite_version_at_least_3_37`).
+- Postgres 15 and 18 are tested (`test_ci_postgres_job_matrix_and_pinned_image`).
+- A Postgres database must use the UTF8 encoding (`test_postgres_non_utf8_database_refused`).
+- U+0000 is held only inside a document, as the six characters of its JSON escape (`test_db_nul_in_verbatim_text_round_trips`).
+- Instants from the year 0001 to the year 9999 round-trip (`test_instant_round_trip_edges`).
+- A stored document is limited to 256 MiB, the limit of the strict loader (unverified).
+
+## 5. Encryption at rest
+
+The database is not encrypted at rest by tracer, so a SQLite file holds the documents as plain text (`test_the_sqlite_file_holds_documents_in_plain_text`).
+
+The stored internal data is personal data: a stored test profile is readable in the file (`test_the_sqlite_file_holds_documents_in_plain_text`).
+
+Encryption of a Postgres server disk is the operator's concern, and tracer does not check it (unverified).
+
+## 6. Digests and the plain profile digest
+
+ADR 0006 Decision 6 states a limitation that holds here: a plain SHA-256 digest of a low-entropy profile in internal data can be brute-forced (`test_policy_documents_low_entropy_digest_limitation`).
+
+The store keeps internal data, so a snapshot whose profile reference has an absent or keyed digest is refused with `InternalSnapshotRefused` (`test_store_run_bundle_refuses_absent_or_keyed_profile_digest`).
+
+A shared export drops the plain digest or keys it with an HMAC (`test_policy_documents_low_entropy_digest_limitation`).
+
+## 7. Deletion and audit
+
+- The roots are `delete_run`, `delete_project`, `delete_test_profile`, `delete_definition`, `delete_dataset_item`, `delete_export` and `delete_snapshot` (`test_delete_run_cascades_every_run_owned_kind`).
+- Every deletion writes one row of `deletion_audit` with no content (`test_deletion_audit_is_content_free`).
+- The `actor` and the `reason` are required, and the reasons are `operator_request`, `retention_policy` and `data_subject_request` (`test_deletion_requires_actor_and_reason`).
+- The audit is append-only (`test_deletion_audit_rows_cannot_be_deleted`).
+- A deletion cascades to what the root owns, and a bundle that lists a deleted member is an `IncompleteRunBundle` (`test_run_bundle_load_reports_incomplete_after_member_deletion`).
+- Retention is recorded and not enforced (`test_no_retention_enforcement_code_exists`).
+
+## 8. Migrations and versions
+
+See `docs/adr/0021-store-schema-version-and-migrations.md`.
+
+Opening a store never migrates it: `open_store` raises `StoreNotMigrated` for a database below the head revision (`test_open_store_at_an_older_shipped_revision_is_not_migrated`).
+
+`upgrade` and `downgrade` are explicit, and a downgrade that would lose rows needs `allow_data_loss` (`test_downgrade_through_0002_to_base_still_asks_for_the_flag_on_a_filled_store`).
+
+The schema version of the data is recorded in `tracer_meta` (`test_tracer_meta_records_schema_version`).
+
+## 9. Phase 5 risks
+
+Storing a bundle of 4,000 turns takes a median of 5.6 to 5.7 s on Postgres through pg8000 `executemany` against 0.28 s on SQLite (finding P2-F4), and no timing threshold is asserted (`test_measurement_harness_runs_on_postgres`).
+
+Concurrent writers are not tested beyond the statement counts, and a loser of a race on the same new record may see a constraint error (unverified).
+
+A change of 0.0.2 that alters the digest of a versioned entity cannot be migrated in place (`test_digest_changing_upgrade_of_versioned_entity_refused`).
+
+## 10. Statements that are not verified
+
+- The version is unreleased and nothing is published (unverified).
+- A stored document is limited to 256 MiB, the limit of the strict loader (unverified).
+- Encryption of a Postgres server disk is the operator's concern, and tracer does not check it (unverified).
+- Concurrent writers are not tested beyond the statement counts, and a loser of a race on the same new record may see a constraint error (unverified).
