+# Changelog: `tracer-evaldb`
+
+Every release lists what the store, its migrations and its policies gained. The data it holds is
+the data of `tracer-evalschema`; the rules of the storage are in `STORAGE_POLICY.md`.
+
+## 0.0.1 (unreleased)
+
+Status: not released. No tag exists and nothing is published.
+
+### Package
+
+- Relational storage of `tracer-evalschema` 0.0.1 on SQLite and Postgres (SQLAlchemy Core and Alembic).
+
+### Storage
+
+- 37 tables, immutability triggers, a deletion audit, `verify_database`. See `STORAGE_POLICY.md`.
+
+### Migrations
+
+- Revisions 0001 (initial schema) and 0002 (access-pattern indexes).
+
+### Findings
+
+- P2-F1: ownership of definitions by project, for 0.0.2.
+- P2-F2: integer bounds of `version` and `*_ms`, for 0.0.2.
+- P2-F3: distinct `span_ref` values within a run, for 0.0.2.
+- P2-F4: the store time of a large bundle on Postgres through pg8000, for Phase 5.
