+# Storage
+
+The `tracer-evaldb` package keeps the entities of `tracer-evalschema` in a relational database. The
+details are decided in [ADR 0019](../adr/0019-relational-storage.md),
+[ADR 0020](../adr/0020-deletion-and-retention.md),
+[ADR 0021](../adr/0021-store-schema-version-and-migrations.md) and
+[ADR 0022](../adr/0022-write-unit-rescoring-reimport.md); the rules are collected in
+`packages/evaldb/STORAGE_POLICY.md`.
+
+## What is stored
+
+One table per entity (26) and eleven side tables. A run bundle is the write unit, stored in one
+transaction (`test_run_bundle_store_is_atomic`).
+
+## Documents and projections
+
+Each row keeps the whole document as text and the columns a query needs, checked against the
+document on every read (`test_db_tampered_doc_rejected_on_read`).
+
+## Two backends, one behaviour
+
+SQLite and Postgres store the same value the same way (`test_storage_policy_parity_table_matches_column_types`).
+
+## What the database does not do
+
+The database is not a validation boundary: the repository is. The database is not encrypted by
+tracer.
+
+## Deletion and retention
+
+Deletion removes what a root owns and writes a content-free audit row. Retention is recorded and not
+enforced.
+
+## Versions and migrations
+
+The store records the schema version of its data and never migrates by being opened.
